<!-- Generated by instrukt from the documentation its index.yaml selects; change that documentation or that index, not this file. -->
This file holds compressed sections. The same instructions in full prose stand in `/home/someone/.instrukt/rendered/claude.uncompressed.md`, which no agent runtime loads; read any snippet this file names in full with `instrukt docs get <id>`.

Compressed sections: a section headed by a document's name holds that document compressed, its rules without its prose. Each line opens with `- `. `MUST` = required, `NEVER` = forbidden, `MAY` = permitted, not required, `PREFER` = the default, which yields to a stated reason; the reason follows ` -- ` in one clause. `<term> = <meaning>` states a term a rule rests on. `->` = leads to or then, `|` = or, `vs` = two forces in tension. Ids, commands, paths, code and configured values stand exactly as in the source. The named document holds the full prose: read it before acting on a case its rules do not name, on its exact wording or on its reasons.

